@* Sync UI: the Devices page on the settings screen, and nothing of another
   context. It talks to the sync client adapters directly - a screen may take an
   adapter - and to its own module's published surface for the feature key, the
   error codes and the pairing-code format.

   Every Backlog.* import is written as @@using global::Backlog.Something, on the
   Dashboard's precedent. This project's root namespace is Backlog.Modules.Sync.UI
   and the Razor generator emits these directives inside that namespace without a
   global:: prefix, so a bare "Backlog" would bind to Backlog.Modules the moment
   anything in this project's reference closure declares a Backlog.Modules.Backlog
   namespace. Nothing does today; global:: means nothing has to keep not doing it. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Sync.Abstractions
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Sync.Abstractions.DataTransferObjects
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Buttons
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Feedback
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Inputs
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Overlays
